nnually. Stock-based compensation of $12K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["HighPeak Energy, Inc. is a small-cap energy business with a $903M market cap on $863M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are contracting by -7.2pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 15% against a 9% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $512M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 59 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 26.98\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -15.3% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 1.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.3% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 82% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -7.2pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":